  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri Niteenpaul Malagi vs Tata Aig General Insurance Co Ltd on 21 November, 2024 -1- Nc: 2024:Khc:47379 Mfa No. 2358 of 2021 C/W Mfa No. 2357 of 2021 In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 21St Day Of November, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Dr. Justice Chillakur Sumalatha Miscellaneous First Appeal No. 2358 Of 2021 (Mv-I) C/W Miscellaneous First Appeal No. 2357 Of 2021 (Mv-I) In Mfa No. 2358/2021 Between: Sri. Tushar Shekhar Chougala, S/O Shekar Chougale, Aged About 22 Years, R/At Indirangara, Near Water Tank, Shiraguppi Village, Athani Taluk, Belagum Dist. - 591 242. ...Appellant (By Sri. M. Nagaraja, Advocate) And: Digitally signed by 1. Tata Aig General Insurance Co. Ltd., Aaseefa Parveen No.60 3Rd Floor, J.P. And Devi Location: High Jambu Keshava Arcade, Court Of Millers Road, Bengaluru - 52. Karnataka 2. Sri. Ramakrishna, S/O Vasudeva Bhatt, No.283, 7Th Main, 15Th Cross, Wilson Garden, Bangalore - 68. ...Respondents (By Sri. N.A. Mallikarjun Reddy, Advocate For Sri. B. Pradeep, Advocate For R1; R2 - Notice Dispensed With Vide Order Dated 23.03.2023) -2- Nc: 2024:Khc:47379 Sri Niteenpaul Malagi vs Tata Aig General Insurance Co Ltd on 21 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/71810683/ 1 Mfa No. 2358 of 2021 C/W Mfa No. 2357 of 2021 This Mfa Is Filed U/S 173(1) Of Mv Act Against The Judgment And Award Dated 12.01.2021 Passed In Mvc No.2604/2019 On The File Of The Xxi Acmm, And Xxiii Ascj, Mact, Bengaluru, Partly Allowing The Claim Petition For Compensation And Seeking Enhancement Of Compensation. In Mfa No. 2357/2021 Between: Sri. Niteenpaul Malagi, S/O Mahaveer, Aged About 24 Years, R/At Waderhatti, Gokak Taluk, Belgaum - 591 224. ...Appellant (By Sri. M. Nagaraja, Advocate) And: 1. Tata Aig General Insurance Co. Ltd., No.60, 3Rd Floor, J.P. And Devi Jambu Keshava Arcade, Millers Road, Bengaluru - 52. 2. SRI. RAMAKRISHNA, S/O VASUDEVA BHATT, NO.283, 7TH MAIN, 15TH CROSS, WILSON GARDEN, BANGALORE - 68. ...RESPONDENTS (BY SRI. N.A. MALLIKARJUN REDDY, ADVOCATE FOR SRI. B. PRADEEP, ADVOCATE FOR R1; R2 - NOTICE DISPENSED WITH VIDE ORDER DATED 23.03.2023) THIS MFA IS FILED U/S 173(1) OF MV ACT AGAINST -3- NC: 2024:KHC:47379 MFA No. 2358 of 2021 C/W MFA No. 2357 of 2021 THE JUDGMENT AND AWARD DATED 12.01.2021 PASSED IN MVC NO.2605/2019 ON THE FILE OF THE XXI ACMM, Sri Niteenpaul Malagi vs Tata Aig General Insurance Co Ltd on 21 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/71810683/ 2 AND XXIII ASCJ, MACT, BENGALURU, PARTLY ALLOWING THE CLAIM PETITION FOR COMPENSATION AND SEEKING ENHANCEMENT OF COMPENSATION. THESE APPEALS, COMING ON FOR ADMISSION, THIS DAY, JUDGMENT WAS DELIVERED THEREIN AS UNDER: CORAM: HON'BLE DR. JUSTICE CHILLAKUR SUMALATHA ORAL JUDGMENT Heard Sri.Nagaraja.M, learned counsel for the appellant in both the appeals as well as Sri.Mallikarjuna Reddy who represents Sri.B.Pradeep, learned counsel on record for respondent No.1 in both the appeals. 2. While MFA No.2358/2021 is filed challenging the order that is rendered in M.V.C. No.2604/2019, MFA No.2357/2021 is filed challenging the order that is rendered in M.V.C. No.2605/2019.",
    "facts": "The tribunal awarded a sum of Rs.3,28,600/- to the claimant in M.V.C. No.2604/2019. It awarded a sum of Rs.3,55,000/- to the claimant in M.V.C. No.2605/2019. However, the tribunal awarded a sum of Rs.10,000/- only under the head 'loss of NC: 2024:KHC:47379 earning during laid up period'. Also the tribunal awarded a sum of Rs.30,000/- only under the head 'pain and suffering'. Through the evidence produced, the appellant established that he incurred a sum of Rs.1,12,135/- for treatment and the tribunal indeed awarded the said amount. However having considered the nature of injuries sustained, this Court is of the view that the appellant would have taken bed rest atleast for a period of 3 months. Also the tribunal awarded a sum of Rs.20,000/- only under the head pain and suffering. The tribunal through the impugned order awarded a sum of Rs.3,55,000/- as compensation divided under following heads:- Heads Amount in Rs. Pain and suffering 20,000-00",
    "arguments": "Contradicting the submission thus made, Sri.Mallikarjuna Reddy, learned counsel for respondent Sri Niteenpaul Malagi vs Tata Aig General Insurance Co Ltd on 21 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/71810683/"
  },
